# What `railway up` uploads to the build.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. `railway up` honours `.gitignore`, and `data/` is
# git-ignored on this project (the corpus, the SQLite registry, the Qdrant
# collection, the parent store and the reports all live there). That meant
# the three corpus PDFs never reached Railway's builder and the image failed
# on `COPY data/corpus /app/seed-corpus` with `"/data/corpus": not found` --
# the whole build otherwise green. Local `docker build` did not catch it,
# because `.dockerignore` re-includes the corpus with `!data/corpus/` and
# the local build context is the working tree, not a git-filtered upload.
#
# So this file takes over the decision for Railway: exclude the heavy,
# machine-specific state under `data/`, and let `data/corpus/` through.

# --- the generated state under data/, none of which belongs in an image ---
# All of it is rebuilt by a Sync, and all of it is specific to whichever
# laptop produced it.
data/qdrant/
data/parents/
data/reports/
data/smoke/
data/spike-st18/
data/sanad.db
data/*.db

# NOTE: data/corpus/ is deliberately NOT listed. It is the seed corpus the
# container copies into the volume on first boot -- without it a deploy has
# no documents and no way to be given any (there is no upload in the UI).

# --- never upload ---
.git/
.venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.env
.env.*
claude-setup.zip
